 "_comment": "Board P r3 draft copper pours (phase 11/12): power-path outlines shaped to floorplan.json, mm in KiCad board coordinates. Read by route-power.py (pours) and route-signals.py (keep other nets out of the power pours). Phase 12: EF_IN starts at x 5.75 so U2.7 (EF_UVLO) can escape; the VBUS_P riser (C3 branch) is x 9.3-11.2 so a 0.2 mm track passes beside the U1 left pins. \"tracks\": fixed stubs placed before routing (U2.6 EF_IN lies between NC U2.5 and U2.7, so the pour cannot reach it). Phase 13: the VBUS_P riser narrows to x 9.3-10.3 for y 21.0-23.5 (it only feeds the C35.2 tap there; the 5 A path runs through x 5.6-9.3), and \"vias\" with their F.Cu stubs fan U1.7 SCL, U1.8 SDA, U1.9 DISCH and U1.11 ATT out to B.Cu: the pour edge had left one 0.1 mm channel for four pins. U2.7 EF_UVLO and U3.1 EF_VCAP get the same fan-out via beside their pads, (5.05, 14.05) and (2.2, 12.5) left of U3.1: the order-dependent router otherwise left them open. The U1.6 RESET strap to R21.1 is a fixed straight track down its own pin corridor. Phase 14: U1.5 CC2DB runs straight up between the R21 pads (0.245 mm to each) to a fixed via at (13.9, 18.6), 0.25 mm from the B.Cu R20.1 pad; U1.4 CC2 takes a fixed via at (14.6, 20.4) in the 1 mm band between the R21.2 pad and the U1 pins (0.22 mm to R21.2). Every tried seed had left one of the two open. U3.3 and U3.6 (both VBUS_IN) are joined by a fixed 0.4 mm F.Cu track between the U3 rows (0.55 mm to U3.2/U3.4/U3.5), so VBUS_IN no longer loops round U3 and U3.2 GND can escape south. U1.2 CC1 has a fixed stub that steps right of the R21.2 pad (0.245 mm) beside the CC2 via.",
